{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0054ed3c9ee5e970855d39c0d6f69518922f4a7aba9c96f19b49b33f963283fd"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The Statistics/Math section features channels such as StatQuest with Josh Starmer, 3Blue1Brown, ritvikmath, zedstatistics, and Brandon Foltz."},{"claim_ids":["clm_327b84eb86e14c223291b7991922130ddcedfa43e0da681a86583aaf7577f3a9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The AI research section lists channels including AI Journal, Arxiv Insights, Yannic Kilcher, Two Minute Papers, and bycloud."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3b011f1ba5a43e9c5e95b7ac4c6f2e2b607c66794d85cacad26f13c68b231bd9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The ML/AI/DL section includes channels like What's AI, Daniel Bourke, Abhishek Thakur, Jay Alammar, AI Coffee Break with Letitia, deeplizard, and Cassie Kozyrkov."},{"claim_ids":["clm_42b1ce7cc02e602badbb2db2eb31b0426a147d856bc6ac1d21ef3a4bfa11d654"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The Organizations section lists official channels including DeepMind, TensorFlow, HuggingFace, OpenAI, PyTorch, Kaggle, DataCamp, and Databricks."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4c322b438f520ca84a743c1e5605ac478771e55e9244a381fa07dd45231454de"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The list includes language-specific sections for Python, R, C++, Julia, Flutter, and Ruby, plus sections for Audio Programming, Cybersecurity, Podcasts/Talks, and Organizations."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5033be358ebda679123f245f8dd9cbecd5628759db3bb0ee199634c522732f4d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The repository is a curated list of over 180 YouTube channels covering data science, machine learning, deep learning, AI, computer science, programming, and software engineering, presented in no particular order."},{"claim_ids":["clm_80e193c8e28ad2026ab9b893e4f6da5a75b3412ea4b9616a8744cffdf66a365c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors are invited to submit pull requests to add more channels to the list."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9461e3bfca2c023984b18f0fab9b6335bcd9efc96df16300aff22dee5c25d6ea"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The Data Science / Data Analysis section lists channels such as Ken Jee, Tina Huang, Data Professor, Krish Naik, Alex The Analyst, and Luke Barousse with YouTube links."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c5861289ee5f9cce6b377ba9a41cff5f5c5db8e7f6058ece1299c6a0d4d9071b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The Podcasts/Talks section includes Lex Fridman, Machine Learning Street Talk, Weights & Biases, Data Skeptic, and DeepLearningAI."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c893a3179bba585406f6c622102b1007f9119094fb155a18a539a171ebbc24bb"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The repository carries an Awesome badge and links to the maintainer's other curated lists, including data science resources for R and a collection of machine learning blogs."},{"claim_ids":["clm_df9223fba5f77b032ac0475e673b3443bfe5620164bcadd6589d4ad15db18b68"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README organizes channels into categories including Data Science, ML/AI/DL, Data Engineering, Statistics/Math, AI research, Computer Science, Programming, Web-dev, and Software Engineering."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0054ed3c9ee5e970855d39c0d6f69518922f4a7aba9c96f19b49b33f963283fd","clm_327b84eb86e14c223291b7991922130ddcedfa43e0da681a86583aaf7577f3a9","clm_3b011f1ba5a43e9c5e95b7ac4c6f2e2b607c66794d85cacad26f13c68b231bd9","clm_42b1ce7cc02e602badbb2db2eb31b0426a147d856bc6ac1d21ef3a4bfa11d654","clm_4c322b438f520ca84a743c1e5605ac478771e55e9244a381fa07dd45231454de","clm_5033be358ebda679123f245f8dd9cbecd5628759db3bb0ee199634c522732f4d","clm_80e193c8e28ad2026ab9b893e4f6da5a75b3412ea4b9616a8744cffdf66a365c","clm_9461e3bfca2c023984b18f0fab9b6335bcd9efc96df16300aff22dee5c25d6ea","clm_c5861289ee5f9cce6b377ba9a41cff5f5c5db8e7f6058ece1299c6a0d4d9071b","clm_c893a3179bba585406f6c622102b1007f9119094fb155a18a539a171ebbc24bb","clm_df9223fba5f77b032ac0475e673b3443bfe5620164bcadd6589d4ad15db18b68"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:38:26Z","created_by_operation":"op_ba3e191a127f435b9e8b9db0